# Secrets and local overrides
.env
*.env
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md

# Local security-remediation working dir (settings backups, scan dumps,
# canary scripts) — contains real/old tokens, never belongs in this repo
security-remediation/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Output (generated daily, don't commit)
# ASK-605: the whole directory, not a list of extensions. auto-commit.py
# declares q-system/output/ skip-because-gitignored; when that claim was
# only true for *.html/*.json/*.log, a .md file there was invisible to the
# hook AND blocked every fleet sync. Keep the negation for .gitkeep so the
# directory survives a clone.
q-system/output/**
!q-system/output/.gitkeep
q-system/output/*.html
q-system/output/*.json
q-system/output/*.log
q-system/output/drafts/*
q-system/output/lead-gen/*
q-system/output/design-partner/*
q-system/output/content-intel/*
q-system/output/investor-updates/*
q-system/output/marketing/linkedin/*
!**/.gitkeep

# Plans (auto-created by Claude Code)
.claude/plans/

# Agent claim-lock: per-working-tree local state. Committing it would share one
# session's claim with every clone and the lock would refuse everyone forever.
.linear-claims.json
.linear-claims.json.guard

# Session transcripts
*.jsonl
# ...but this one is not a transcript, it is the repo's own closure-evidence
# ledger. test-updater-issue-sequence.py audits it against real commit ancestry,
# and the blanket ignore above meant it never reached a fresh clone -- so in CI
# every issue read as "no closure receipt" while passing locally off an untracked
# working copy. Verified 2026-07-26: structural ids and timestamps only, no
# free-text, safe for a public repo.
!.prd-os/receipts.jsonl

# SQLite databases (generated at runtime)
*.db

# Generated sites and build output
sites/
template-repo/

# Bus data (daily pipeline, ephemeral)
q-system/.q-system/agent-pipeline/bus/

# Obsidian vault config (user-specific, not committed)
q-system/.obsidian/

# Raw source transcripts (instance-specific, 90-day retention)
q-system/sources/*.md

# Pruned markdown archives (historical, not loaded in context)
q-system/memory/archives/

# Session-scoped recall artifact for memory auto-capture (PRD prd-memory-autocapture)
q-system/memory/.session-recall.json
q-system/memory/.session-recall.json.lock
q-system/memory/.session-recall.json.tmp-*

# Node
node_modules/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# prd-os runtime state (per plugins/prd-os/skills/prd-os/SKILL.md: never committed)
#
# pr-receipts/ is a MACHINE-LOCAL claim about a machine-local test run (Codex
# major, PR #269 round 7). It is meaningless to anyone else -- it names a sha and
# says "the floor was run here" -- and this fleet's unattended jobs commit with
# `git add -A`, so an unignored receipt directory rides into the public repo and
# then looks like a receipt everybody agreed to.
.prd-os/pr-receipts/
.claude/state/active-prd.json
.claude/state/active-issue.json
.claude/state/prdos-stop-gate-firings.json

# Generated standalone plugin builds
plugins/*/dist/
/dist/

# Session artifacts (browser automation logs, daily update stamps)
.playwright-mcp/
q-system/output/.update-check-*

# Codex CLI local config. Holds real credentials -- Pure_spectrum_Q's
# .codex/config.toml carries an apify-token, which gitleaks correctly refused
# to let through on 2026-07-25. Machine-local tool config, never repo content.
.codex/

# Session bookkeeping written by the kipi-dsse stop gate: created while an
# issue is open, removed when it closes, so tracking it churned git on every
# DSSE cycle and committed one session's firing counts.
.claude/state/

# Generated capability maps (regenerate with capability-map-gen.py; ~5MB, churns
# on every run). The committed artifact is the digest the overlap pass emits.
q-system/output/capability-maps/
.runs/

# Lock files beside the prd-os ledgers. flock targets, recreated on every
# resolve/reclassify, and they were standing untracked-and-unignored inside a
# TRACKED directory. sp-a21cb27c predicted an unattended auto-commit would sweep
# them in; measured 2026-08-14 that is false -- auto-commit.py's NEVER list
# already refuses any .lock, so system_state_paths returns [] for both. What was
# left was permanent noise in `git status`, which is its own cost: a status that
# is never clean is a status nobody reads.
.prd-os/*.lock
.prd-os/.judgments.lock

# THE STANZA BETWEEN THESE MARKERS IS SHIPPED TO EVERY INSTANCE (sp-097d2e23).
# kipi-update-gitignore-block.py parses it out of this file and writes it into
# each instance's root .gitignore as a managed block. Root .gitignore is not in
# the updater's sync set, so until 2026-08-14 these rules existed only here --
# and an instance that does not ignore these paths has git report them, which
# hands them straight to auto-commit.py (q-system/.q-system/ classifies as
# "chore", which the fleet sync commits unattended). Five of 22 instances had
# already committed their own baseline or armed marker, the most recent that
# same day. Add a path here and every instance gets it on the next update; the
# writer refuses rather than guessing if these markers ever go missing.
# >>> kipi-instance-local-stanza >>>
# .claude/ integrity baseline is INSTANCE-LOCAL (ASK-282). Never commit it:
# kipi update propagates the skeleton, but each instance regenerates
# .claude/settings.json from settings-template.json, so a shared baseline can
# never match and would Slack-page every instance daily.
q-system/.q-system/claude-integrity-baseline.json
q-system/.q-system/claude-integrity-baseline.json.lock
q-system/output/claude-integrity/
# The armed marker (ASK-291 round 11) is ignored for the SAME reason and it is
# load-bearing that it stays that way: a committed marker propagates via kipi
# update, so every fresh instance would claim prior arming, refuse to arm, and
# Slack-page SECURITY on its first run -- the round-2 outage exactly.
q-system/.q-system/.claude-integrity-armed
# Daily update stamps. Pure updater exhaust, and the reason this line moved
# into the shipped stanza: instances carry hundreds of them, many already
# committed by the pre-ASK-498 generic-fallback sweep.
q-system/output/.update-check-*
# <<< kipi-instance-local-stanza <<<

# PR-review scratch trees. 537 of these files were swept into the repo by an
# unattended `chore: update project files` auto-commit (ec5efddf). Removing them
# without ignoring the pattern just waits for the next sweep to re-add them.
.pr*rev*/
.review-scratch/
.fable-wt/

# Agent refusal sentinels. These are TRANSIENT and worktree-local: the agent
# writes one, the worker reads it, labels the issue, and deletes it. Committing
# one is a live defect, not clutter -- on merge it lands at the root of main, so
# every worktree cut from main afterwards materializes it at checkout BEFORE any
# agent runs. The worker then reads a sentinel it did not write and refuses an
# unrelated issue, carrying the previous issue's reason text into that issue's
# Linear comment and needs-scope label.
#
# Observed on PR #141 (ASK-700): a refusal was written here and swept in by
# `git add -A`. The ignore is the fix rather than a review checklist -- a path
# `git add -A` cannot stage cannot be committed by any future agent on any
# future branch. Asserted by case 13 of test-worker-refusal.sh.
.sana-needs-scope
.sana-blocked-capability
.codex-blocked-capability
#
# The per-issue PR body the loop writes for `gh pr create`. Same mechanism as the
# sentinels above and the same fix, but lower stakes: nothing READS a stale PR
# body, so a swept-in one is clutter rather than a live defect (sp-b2a5e5be,
# from ASK-700). Anchored to the repo root because that is the only place the
# loop writes it -- a bare glob would also hide a real file someone adds under a
# subdirectory later. Asserted by test_gitignore_agent_scratch.py.
/.pr-body-*.md
